COLOR PALETTE GUIDANCE
The primary color is used as the cover page background and section divider background. Choose a rich, dark, topic-appropriate color that communicates the tutorial domain. For coding/software topics, prefer deep navy, slate, graphite, or terminal-inspired dark green with a clean accent.

Example palettes:
  Frontend/UI tutorial      primary #182033  accent #7dd3fc
  Backend/API tutorial      primary #102a43  accent #38bdf8
  AI/LLM tutorial           primary #231942  accent #c084fc
  DevOps/deployment guide   primary #172554  accent #f59e0b
  Debugging walkthrough     primary #1f2937  accent #f97316
  Default software topic    primary #111827  accent #60a5fa

Broad-topic fallback palettes when the life_event/tutorial request is not software-focused:
  Legal / policy tutorial   primary #1e2d40  accent #c9a84c
  Caregiving tutorial       primary #1a3a2a  accent #7aab8a
  Medical / health tutorial primary #242424  accent #4a9e8e
  Financial tutorial        primary #1a2340  accent #d4a017
  Default / other tutorial  primary #1a1a1a  accent #b8a97a

You MUST still return every field in the full color_palette object. Choose suitable light values for background, surface, text_primary, text_secondary, and border.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
